text:
[Trigger warning] A year and a half ago, I met a guy at a bar and things happened

First off, I want to apologize. I don't why know, I just feel like I should apologize.

&amp;#x200B;

When I was in college about a year and a half ago, I went to a bar crawl with a few of my friends. It was ladies night and drinks were free. I never drink too much, especially in public. I had maybe 2 drinks and my friends and I were always together. These 2 guys approached us and started talking. I was interested in one of them and we started talking, dancing, laughing... I felt like I really liked him. We exchanged numbers and talked. I was so excited about meeting someone because I was always very shy and very focused on my studies, so meeting guys was not on my list of priorities. I called my mom the next morning, so excited about meeting someone since I was very stressed about school at the time and finally had a time to have fun.

&amp;#x200B;

The next time we met, he invited me to his place to watch a horror movie. He offered me a beer in which I only had a sip or two of because I had driven myself there and hadn't planned on staying the night. Then, we went to his bedroom to watch the movie. Halfway through, we started making out. Then, he took off my pants. I kept telling him not since I was on my period, so I would pull them back up and he would pull them down again. I had never had sex at that point, so I wasn't ready. He kept trying and started thrusting, but he did it against my underwear, so I didn't think much of it. When I left, I felt disgusted with myself, but for some reason I did not realize the red flags (I was inexperienced with dating and at that stage in my life, just felt like it was normal I guess). A week later, he invites me to a concert with him so I, his friend, and one of my friends went. He had way too many drinks and put his hands around my neck. I hated it and played it cool so he wouldn't get aggressive and my friend and I left, waiting outside at 1am in a snowstorm in the cold and called another friend of ours to pick us up an hour away.

&amp;#x200B;

A year and a half later, I think about that. I have a boyfriend who is very sweet and ALWAYS asks for consent and even reminds me during that if I don't want it, to let him know. Until I met him, I guess I didn't know what a healthy, consensual relationship was and I think about that man that I went on a few dates with. I have never told ANYBODY about what happened that night I went on a date with him and we watched a movie... mostly because I feel embarrassed by it. I feel like it was MY fault and not his for putting myself in that situation. I was inexperienced and just excited to be seeing somebody since I had never really dated anyone. Now, whenever I go downtown to the area where we went to the concert, I feel sickened by it. My sister and I went to a sports game there a year ago and I felt sick. My best friends knows about that particular situation, but nothing else. No one
